Description: Do not select the row under a resting pointer when the window opens
 With hover-select, rofi_view_ping_mouse() made the row under the mouse pointer the selection as soon as the window
 was created. The pointer had not moved, and typing kept that row instead of the best match: with the pointer resting
 in the middle of the screen, typing "display settings" + Enter opened another entry. The position and the cursor are
 still taken over; the first real motion event selects as before.
Author: Simple OS <https://github.com/FreakySneaky787/Simple-OS>
Bug: https://github.com/FreakySneaky787/Simple-OS/issues/144
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-21

--- a/source/view.c	2026-11-21 09:45:33.209165654 +0100
+++ b/source/view.c	2026-11-21 09:45:33.222809099 +0100
@@ -1980,8 +1980,11 @@
     return;
   }
 
+  // Simple OS: only set the pointer position and cursor here, never select the row under a resting pointer. With
+  // hover-select the row under the pointer became the selection when the window opened, and typing kept that row
+  // instead of the best match (Simple OS issue #144). The first real pointer motion selects as before.
   rofi_view_handle_mouse_motion(state, pointer_reply->win_x,
-                                pointer_reply->win_y, config.hover_select);
+                                pointer_reply->win_y, FALSE);
 
   free(pointer_reply);
 }
